-- title:
--   Node depth of inertia-fixed places is a power of v_A(q)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an integer $N \ge 1$, a perfect field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$. Let `data` be a modular polynomial datum for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the pair of $q$-expansions of $j$) satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X^q - Y)(X - Y^q)$ modulo $q$, and let `hα`, `hβ` assert that the two degeneracy embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` from level $N$ to level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ are integral. Let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data, $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$, $K$ an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, and $w$ a place of the level-$N$ modular function field over $k$. Let $c$ be a node-coordinate datum for $R$ at $w$ over $K$: elements $x, y$ of the ring `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` (functions integral for both prolongations $R₁, R₂$ and for every place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(Nq))$ reducing to $w$, whose Laurent expansions lie in the subfield generated by $K$-constants and the relevant $q$-expansions of $j$) with first residue of $x$ zero, second residue of $x$ of order $1$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, second residue of $y$ zero, and first residue of $y$ of order $1$ at $w$. Assume: the value-integrality law for $R$ at $w$, namely that $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\, f \in A$ for all $f$ in `R.nodeIntegers w` and all places $V$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(Nq))$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\, V = w$; that every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ fixes $K$ pointwise; a nonzero $\varpi \in A \cap K$; a natural number $E$ and a unit $u$ of `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` with $x y = (\text{constant }\varpi)^E u$. Then for every place $V$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(Nq))$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\, V = w$ such that the residue field of $V$ is generated by $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $V$ is fixed by the arithmetic Galois action of every inertia element, there is $d \in \mathbb N$ with $c.\mathrm{yDepth}\, V = A.\mathrm{valuation}(q)^d$, where $c.\mathrm{yDepth}\, V$ is the value of the valuation of $A$ at $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\, y$.
--
--   This is the integrality of the depth of an inertia-fixed point in the annulus above a node of the reduction of $X_0(Nq)$ at $q$: the position of such a point, measured by the valuation of the node coordinate $y$ at it, is an integral power of the valuation of $q$. It feeds the construction of prolongation tuples with node coordinates and depth data used in the analysis of the special fibre at $q$.
